# Soul carryover items (life/carryover.js, design/data/carryover.toml, master plan §4, sprint3-4.md S1). The strip of
# the ender chest and Curios is covered by carryover.rcon; this test is about what a soul gets: the Soul Gem and the
# Remembered Enchantment. `ttl soul expect <bot> <field> <value>` (and `... has <item> <value>`) print "ttl: ..." when
# wrong, which `server.sh test-all` counts as a failure. Bots fake their Life 1 deeds with `ttl karma <bot> set`.
# Bots: C = Craft-heavy Hero (gets the book), H = Hero whose best side is not Craft (no book), N = Wanderer.
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] soul: TtlBotSoulC Life 1 death,
# best enchantment minecraft:sharpness 5", "[ttl] soul: TtlBotSoulC remembers minecraft:sharpness 3",
# "[ttl] soul: TtlBotSoulH Life 1 death, best enchantment minecraft:sharpness 4" and no "remembers" line for H and N,
# "[ttl] soul: TtlBotSoulC gem echo (20s, level 2)".
ttlbot spawn TtlBotSoulC
ttlbot spawn TtlBotSoulH
ttlbot spawn TtlBotSoulN
@sleep 4
ttl soul TtlBotSoulC clear
ttl soul TtlBotSoulH clear
ttl soul TtlBotSoulN clear
# Every Life 1 soul holds exactly one Soul Gem (the login hook, or `give` when the bot was too quick for it).
ttl soul TtlBotSoulC give
ttl soul TtlBotSoulH give
ttl soul TtlBotSoulN give
ttl soul TtlBotSoulC give
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC gem 1
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC flag yes
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC memory no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC has soul_gem yes
# The echo is dormant in Life 1 (a refusal would print "ttl: ..." here, so the hook is not called): no cooldown yet.
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC cooling no
# C: an enchanted book in the ender chest, a diamond in a backpack-less Curios slot, a diamond on the body.
item replace entity TtlBotSoulC enderchest.0 with minecraft:enchanted_book[minecraft:stored_enchantments={levels:{"minecraft:sharpness":5,"minecraft:unbreaking":3}}]
ttl stash TtlBotSoulC equip minecraft:diamond
give TtlBotSoulC minecraft:diamond 2
give TtlBotSoulC minecraft:diamond_pickaxe[minecraft:enchantments={levels:{"minecraft:efficiency":4,"minecraft:binding_curse":1}}]
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC ender 1
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC curios 1
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC has diamond yes
# C is a Hero whose Craft axis is by far its strongest: a month of play, 400 + 400 diamonds, ancient debris, anvils.
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC set play_time 720000
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC set diamond_ore 400
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC set deepslate_diamond_ore 400
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC set ancient_debris 200
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC set anvil 600
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC set smithing 300
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC expect tier elite
# H is a Hero through fighting, trading and learning; its Craft axis is weak (and a sword is its best enchantment).
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH set play_time 720000
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH set mob_kills 300
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH set far 3000
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH set nether 1
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH set trades 60
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH set deepslate_diamond_ore 30
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH set enchants 15
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH set advancements 35
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH expect tier elite
give TtlBotSoulH minecraft:diamond_sword[minecraft:enchantments={levels:{"minecraft:sharpness":4}}]
give TtlBotSoulH minecraft:diamond 2
# N is a fresh Wanderer with an enchanted tool: it remembers it, but a Wanderer earns no book.
give TtlBotSoulN minecraft:iron_pickaxe[minecraft:enchantments={levels:{"minecraft:efficiency":3}}]
# The soulbound gem cannot be thrown away in Life 1: the drop is cancelled (verify by hand: Q on the gem).
# Life 1 death: the gem is kept by the soulbound tag, the best enchantment is remembered, the body is stripped.
kill TtlBotSoulC
kill TtlBotSoulH
kill TtlBotSoulN
@sleep 2
ttl inspect TtlBotSoulC
ttl soul TtlBotSoulC
ttl stash TtlBotSoulC expect kept 1
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC gem 0
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC ender empty
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC curios empty
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC has diamond no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC memory yes
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC book no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulH memory yes
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulN memory yes
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulN gem 0
# Rebirth. C and H are Heroes (pick 1 of 3 uniques), N a Wanderer who is reborn at once.
execute as TtlBotSoulC run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotSoulC run ttl choose slime
execute as TtlBotSoulH run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotSoulH run ttl choose slime
execute as TtlBotSoulN run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotSoulN run ttl choose slime
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC expect step unique
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC pick
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH expect step unique
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH pick
@sleep 1
ttl karma TtlBotSoulC expect phase life2
ttl karma TtlBotSoulH expect phase life2
ttl karma TtlBotSoulN expect phase life2
ttl inspect TtlBotSoulC
ttl soul TtlBotSoulC
# Everyone holds exactly one (re-issued) Soul Gem, nothing else of the old body, and the memory is used up.
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC gem 1
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulH gem 1
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulN gem 1
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC memory no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulH memory no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulN memory no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC has diamond no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC has diamond_pickaxe no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC ender empty
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC curios empty
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulH has diamond_sword no
# Only the Craft-heavy Hero is reborn with the Remembered Enchantment (Sharpness V remembered as Sharpness III).
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC book 1
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC has enchanted_book yes
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulH book no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulH has enchanted_book no
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulN book no
# Life 2: the gem's echo works once, then it rests (the second `use` would print "ttl: ..." so only the state is checked).
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC cooling no
ttl soul TtlBotSoulC use
ttl soul expect TtlBotSoulC cooling yes
# Cleanup
ttl soul TtlBotSoulC clear
ttl soul TtlBotSoulH clear
ttl soul TtlBotSoulN clear
ttl reset TtlBotSoulC
ttl reset TtlBotSoulH
ttl reset TtlBotSoulN
ttlbot remove TtlBotSoulC
ttlbot remove TtlBotSoulH
ttlbot remove TtlBotSoulN
